<h2>How should the grouped settings page be laid out?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">The same 12 fields in four groups: Profile, Preferences, Notifications, Security. Every option keeps one form and one Save button.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A: Stacked sections</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px">
          <div class="label">Profile</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Display name">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Email">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Avatar URL">
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Preferences</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Time zone">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Language">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Theme">
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Notifications</div>
          <div>[x] Email &nbsp; [ ] Push &nbsp; [x] Weekly digest</div>
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Security</div>
          <div>[ ] Two-factor auth</div>
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Session timeout (min)">
          <input class="mock-input" placeholder="API token">
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Stacked sections</h3>
      <p>One column with a heading per group. Simplest change, HTML and CSS only. Still a long page, but easy to scan.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B: Two-column sections</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px">
            <div style="width:35%"><strong>Profile</strong><br><span style="opacity:.6">How others see you</span></div>
            <div style="flex:1"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Display name"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Email"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Avatar URL"></div>
          </div>
          <hr>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px">
            <div style="width:35%"><strong>Preferences</strong><br><span style="opacity:.6">Locale and appearance</span></div>
            <div style="flex:1"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Time zone"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Language"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Theme"></div>
          </div>
          <hr>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px">
            <div style="width:35%"><strong>Notifications</strong></div>
            <div style="flex:1">[x] Email<br>[ ] Push<br>[x] Weekly digest</div>
          </div>
          <hr>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px">
            <div style="width:35%"><strong>Security</strong></div>
            <div style="flex:1">[ ] Two-factor auth<input class="mock-input" placeholder="Session timeout"><input class="mock-input" placeholder="API token"></div>
          </div>
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Two-column sections</h3>
      <p>Group title and a short description on the left, fields on the right. More structured, and wants a wider container (~820px). Collapses to one column on narrow screens. HTML and CSS only.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C: Sidebar tabs</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px">
          <div style="display:flex">
            <div class="mock-sidebar" style="width:30%"><strong>Profile</strong><br>Preferences<br>Notifications<br>Security</div>
            <div class="mock-content" style="flex:1">
              <div class="label">Profile</div>
              <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Display name">
              <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Email">
              <input class="mock-input" placeholder="Avatar URL">
              <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C. Sidebar tabs</h3>
      <p>Shows one group at a time. Shortest page, but it needs JS for switching tabs, and fields on hidden tabs are easy to forget. Likely more than 12 fields need.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
